{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778976493271,"sessionID":"ses_1ccbea798ffeJ0uzdzxLz5j3hi","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_U3BN5vncJZc739Am2gvtNHQy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Added explicit `in taxon: Mus musculus` constraints for DN2a thymocyte (CL_0002423) and DN2b thymocyte (CL_0002424). Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+## Summary\n+\n+Added explicit mouse taxon constraints to the two requested thymocyte terms:\n+\n+- `CL_0002423` DN2a thymocyte now has `in taxon: Mus musculus`.\n+- `CL_0002424` DN2b thymocyte now has `in taxon: Mus musculus`.\n+\n+Each new axiom is annotated with the originating tracker issue: `https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3500`.\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+The existing term comments already state that DN2a and DN2b thymocytes are observed in mice and caution that double-negative thymocyte markers differ across species. The requested explicit taxon restrictions make that modeling machine-readable and prevent these marker-defined mouse subsets from being interpreted as general cross-species thymocyte classes.\n+\n+I did not remove `human_subset` annotations because no `human_subset` annotations were present for `CL_0002423` or `CL_0002424` in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- Reviewed the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Inspected the DN2a and DN2b entries in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Checked existing `in taxon` patterns using `RO_0002162` and `NCBITaxon_10090`.\n+- Checked for existing `human_subset` annotations on the affected terms.\n+- Reviewed the cited PubMed records sufficiently to confirm that the requested mouse restriction is supported, especially PMID:20543111 and PMID:25060579.\n+- Validated ontology syntax with `robot convert --input src/ontology/cl-edit.o